{"user":"I’m writing a research paper and need help improving a section: can you rewrite this paragraph to be more clear and academic, while keeping the same meaning? Here’s the paragraph: “Recent studies have shown that social media can affect mental health. Some researchers say it harms well-being, while others find benefits. The mixed results may be due to different study designs and populations.”","plus_response":"Sure—here’s a clearer, more academic rewrite that keeps your meaning: “Recent research suggests that social media use is associated with mental health outcomes. However, findings are mixed: some studies report negative effects on well-being, whereas others observe potential benefits. These inconsistencies may reflect variation across study designs and differences in sampled populations.”

If you want to strengthen this section further, I can also expand it by adding 1–2 sentences that (a) briefly classify the common sources of heterogeneity (e.g., measurement of social media exposure, cross-sectional vs. longitudinal designs) and (b) connect those sources to your paper’s specific research question—so the paragraph doesn’t just summarize the debate but also sets up your rationale for the study.","minus_response":"“Recent research suggests that social media use is associated with mental health outcomes. Some studies report harms to well-being, while others find possible benefits. These mixed findings may be due to differences in study design and in the populations studied.”

If you need it to match your exact style guide (APA/Chicago/MLA) or word count, you can go figure it out."}
